From: inkwell (block PU1c, rule P-13) — proposed for oioio-space/go-libp2p on cae49c803966 and upstream
Subject: [PATCH] quicreuse: configure and account for initial receive windows

Unread stream bytes hold QUIC connection credit. Applications that order their
inbound streams need an initial connection window larger than the combined
windows of the streams they leave unread, and a resource reservation before a
peer can consume that credit.

- quicreuse.InitialReceiveWindows(stream, conn) sets the initial stream and
  connection receive windows. The maximum windows and auto-tuning still apply.
- quicreuse.AccountInitialConnectionWindow(rm) opens and charges the inbound
  resource scope in ConnContext, before quic-go constructs the connection. The
  accepted connection reuses the scope and its reservation. The QUIC context
  and libp2p close paths release the scope once. Outbound QUIC reserves its
  initial window after SetPeer and before the dial. A failed reservation
  refuses the connection. The option is off by default.

Apply with git apply on oioio-space/go-libp2p cae49c803966
(v0.51.1-0.20261109121346-cae49c803966). Inkwell uses a local replace until the
integrator publishes the fork and pins its new pseudo-version.

